From ebfe9817ed9a9378e5f84bc67e49e2d5906abb03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 23:24:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): revert runtime Beads read; fence titles;
 word-boundary routing (W1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the release-check regression + 5 review threads on the W1 head:
- Revert the runtime Beads/bd read in prime live-state — Beads is retired from
  the runtime (migration-only), so there is NO runtime Beads live-data source;
  Kernel is the sole backend, gated on an existing DB (read-only). Fixes the
  forge release check "Beads retirement" gate that failed on all platforms.
- Fence the claimed-issue title with fenceUntrusted (same guard as the memory
  digest) + clip/normalize values before interpolation — closes a prompt-
  injection vector in the session-entry Live State.
- Match single-word routing keywords on a word boundary ("please" no longer
  misroutes to claim-safety via the "lease" substring).
- Point the Cursor always-apply rule at the installed .cursor/skills mirror /
  by name, not a repo-relative skills/ path.
- Drop the super-linear name: regex (SonarCloud) for startsWith+slice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
